	"FriendlyName": "PoiseBreak - Poise, Stagger Tiers & Hyper Armor",
	"Description": "Whether a hit staggers should not depend on how big the hit was. It should depend on how close the target already was to breaking - that is what makes a fight feel like a fight instead of a lottery. PoiseBreak keeps a poise pool per actor and decides the break from the OVERSHOOT: the same twenty points of poise damage does nothing to a fresh enemy and knocks down one that had five left. Breaks come in tiers, each with its own stagger length and its own immunity window - and the immunity covers the stagger, because four attackers who each land a flinch must not hold an actor still forever. Hyper armor scales incoming poise damage during your attack windows without touching health damage. Poise regenerates after a delay that every hit resets, and never while the actor is staggered. Every rule is a pure function that the component and the tests both call, so what you see on the meter cannot disagree with the plugin.",
